From cebf017cef1e46a9df7ad287a662a79041c79a09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:03:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Package the vendored robin-map licence

src_cpp/lsd.hpp and union_find.hpp #include tessil/robin-map
(include/robin_map), vendored with its licence embedded only in the
header comments; no separate COPYING/LICENSE file travels with it for
setuptools' default license_files glob to pick up, so no ldpc wheel on
any architecture (including upstream's own PyPI ones) ships that
licence text.

Adding a root LICENSE.robin-map (the exact text embedded in
robin_hash.h et al.) reaches dist-info/licenses/ with no other
packaging change: ldpc declares no explicit license-files list, so
setuptools' PEP 639 default LICEN[CS]E*/COPYING*/NOTICE*/AUTHORS* glob
already applies.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; the same gap exists in every ldpc wheel on PyPI regardless of architecture, so this needs a maintainer discussion rather than a drive-by PR]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 LICENSE.robin-map | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.robin-map

diff --git a/LICENSE.robin-map b/LICENSE.robin-map
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e9c5ae9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/LICENSE.robin-map
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
